-- title:
--   Fundamental identity ef=[K_w:ℚ_q] for R_w
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number carrying the hypothesis that it is prime, and let $K_w$ be an intermediate field of the extension $\mathbb{Q}_q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ (the algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl q`) which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_q$. Write $R_w$ for `Rw q Kw`, the valuation subring of $K_w$ obtained by pulling back, along the structure map $K_w \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$, the valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ attached to its $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$-valued valuation; that is, $R_w = \{x \in K_w : |x| \le 1\}$, the ring of integers of $K_w$. The assertion is that there exist natural numbers $e$ and $f$, both strictly positive, such that: the ideal of $R_w$ generated by the image of the natural number $q$ equals the $e$-th power of the maximal ideal of the local ring $R_w$; the residue field of $R_w$ has cardinality (as a natural number, via `Nat.card`) equal to $q^f$; and $e \cdot f$ equals the $\mathbb{Q}_q$-dimension of $K_w$.
--
--   This is the fundamental identity $ef = [K_w:\mathbb{Q}_q]$ relating ramification index and residue degree for the unique prime of the ring of integers of a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$. It supplies the ramification and residue data used downstream in the local analysis at $q$, for instance in the statements about roots of minimal polynomials over the residue field and about principal units of $R_w$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ExtCitation_LocalLevel_exists_ramification_inertia_Rw.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ExtCitation_LocalLevelResidues

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false
open ExtCitation.LocalLevel

theorem ExtCitation.LocalLevel.exists_ramification_inertia_Rw (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime]
    (Kw : IntermediateField ℚ_[q] (PadicAlgCl q)) [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[q] Kw] :
    ∃ e f : ℕ, 0 < e ∧ 0 < f ∧
      Ideal.span {((q : ℕ) : Rw q Kw)} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Rw q Kw) ^ e ∧
      Nat.card (IsLocalRing.ResidueField (Rw q Kw)) = q ^ f ∧
      e * f = Module.finrank ℚ_[q] Kw := by sorry
